---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
---
<ProjectLayout
  title="LinkedIn Video"
  subtitle="Owning end-to-end design for LinkedIn’s short-form video experience and driving product direction in a fast-moving, high-priority company investment."
  description="LinkedIn Video case study by Kenny Raymond — leading end-to-end design for LinkedIn's short-form video experience and driving product direction across the company."
  ogImage="/Videohero.png"
>

  <!-- Hero image -->
  <section data-no-reveal class="project-hero-section px-3 md:px-36 lg:px-64">
    <img
      src="/Videohero.png"
      alt="LinkedIn Video hero"
      class="w-full h-auto rounded-[48px]"
    />
  </section>

  <!-- Overview -->
  <section class="px-3 md:px-36 lg:px-64 py-14 md:py-20">
    <h2 class="text-[2.8rem] md:text-[3.4rem] leading-[1] md:leading-[1.1] font-semibold text-white mt-4 mb-3 max-w-3xl mx-auto">Overview</h2>
    <p class="text-white text-2xl md:text-[1.69rem] leading-snug mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      After launching the video tab, video quickly became one of LinkedIn’s fastest growing formats, but the early product thesis was still forming. I led design across the end-to-end short-form video experience and partnered closely with product, engineering, data science, editorial, and senior leadership to help define what short-form video should mean in a professional context.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- GIF -->
  <section class="flex justify-center px-6 py-10 md:py-16">
    <img
      src="/tab.gif"
      alt="LinkedIn Video tab interface"
      class="w-72 md:w-80 h-auto rounded-2xl"
    />
  </section>

  <!-- Problem -->
  <section class="px-3 md:px-36 lg:px-64 py-14 md:py-20">
    <h2 class="text-[2.8rem] md:text-[3.4rem] leading-[1] md:leading-[1.1] font-semibold text-white mt-4 mb-3 max-w-3xl mx-auto">Problem</h2>
    <p class="text-white text-2xl md:text-[1.69rem] leading-snug mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      Early adoption was strong, but retention showed we had not yet built a product people consistently wanted to return to. The experience was useful, but it leaned heavily on informational content and lacked a distinct point of view from other short-form platforms. We needed to move quickly from “video exists on LinkedIn” to “video has a clear reason to belong on LinkedIn.”
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- My role -->
  <section class="px-3 md:px-36 lg:px-64 py-14 md:py-20">
    <h2 class="text-[2.8rem] md:text-[3.4rem] leading-[1] md:leading-[1.1] font-semibold text-white mt-4 mb-3 max-w-3xl mx-auto">My role</h2>
    <p class="text-white text-2xl md:text-[1.69rem] leading-snug mx-auto mb-6 max-w-3xl">
      As design lead, I owned the end-to-end experience across the immersive player and key entry points in feed, profile, and search. I explored multiple product directions, drove alignment across 30+ stakeholders, and translated ambiguous product questions into concrete interaction models, surfaces, and experiments the team could ship and learn from.
    </p>
    <p class="text-white text-2xl md:text-[1.69rem] leading-snug mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      I also stepped into an acting PM role for six months, helping guide prioritization, experiment decisions, and cross-team alignment while continuing to lead design.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Approach -->
  <section class="px-3 md:px-36 lg:px-64 py-14 md:py-20">
    <h2 class="text-[2.8rem] md:text-[3.4rem] leading-[1] md:leading-[1.1] font-semibold text-white mt-4 mb-3 max-w-3xl mx-auto">Approach</h2>
    <p class="text-white text-2xl md:text-[1.69rem] leading-snug mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      I pushed the team to look beyond ranking and relevance and ask a more fundamental question: what makes short-form video on LinkedIn different? After exploring different directions, we landed on the concept of workplace trends — prompts that invited creators to share opinions around professional conversations.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Mockup images -->
  <section class="px-3 md:px-8 py-10 md:py-14">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 md:gap-8 items-center justify-center">
      <img
        src="/video mock left.png"
        alt="LinkedIn Video mockup — feed view"
        class="w-full md:flex-1 md:min-w-0 h-auto rounded-[40px]"
      />
      <img
        src="/video mock right.png"
        alt="LinkedIn Video mockup — profile view"
        class="w-full md:flex-1 md:min-w-0 h-auto rounded-[40px]"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Impact -->
  <section class="px-3 md:px-36 lg:px-64 py-14 md:py-20">
    <h2 class="text-[2.8rem] md:text-[3.4rem] leading-[1] md:leading-[1.1] font-semibold text-white mt-4 mb-3 max-w-3xl mx-auto">Impact</h2>
    <p class="text-white text-2xl md:text-[1.69rem] leading-snug mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      The work contributed to meaningful gains in engagement, including a 2.5× lift in daily retention and nearly 3× growth in carousel CTR. It also helped elevate video into a top company priority and established the foundation for continued investment in discovery, creator participation, and platform quality.
    </p>
  </section>

</ProjectLayout>
